></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:t/></a:r><a:endParaRPr b="0" i="0" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="487" name="Google Shape;487;p68"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="304800" y="1447800"/><a:ext cx="8382000" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" type="none" w="med"/><a:tailEnd len="med" type="none" w="med"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="The first elongation step in bacteria, where binding of the second aminoacyl-tRNA occurs.
This begins with a large yellow subunit labeled as 50S. The subunit has a three-columned scalloped cut out.  Bonded below is a small orange subunit, labeled as 30S. At the top of this subunit, it has a three-column cut out. In the large subunit on the left, it is labeled as E and on the right is A. In the middle is the elongated intertwined green structure with a yellow base, and a blue sphere labeled as tMet. Below The base is labeled as UAC. Below this is an mRNA line that curves through and extends right. It begins with light green, then dark orange, then light green, then a dark green section with AUG just under the UAC base. This is the start of codon, which is followed by a short yellow section labeled as, “next codon”. From here, it is light green and ends with 3’. Below this is an arrow to a replica of the same image, but there is a second elongated intertwined green structure which is angled to the right. This has a blue sphere on top labeled as AA2. This has an arrow pointing back and down to A. Also on the right base of the large subunit is a purple circle, labeled as Tu. Below this is a down arrow labeled as GTP hydrolysis and accommodation. This has an an arrow jutting down and right to Tu in a purple circle. From here, a series of arrows forms a circle back to the Tu on the image. The Tu with the arrow jutting to it bonds right to GDP [plus]Pi. From here an arrow points to a brown circle with Ts on the left bonded to the Tu circle on the right. Tangenting to this arrow is a curved arrow from Ts in a brown circle to GDP. From the Ts/Tu circle has an arrow pointing up to Tu in a circle, which bonds right to GTP. GTP joins this arrow and another arrow jutting right to Ts in a brown circle. From the Tu which bonds to GTP is another arrow pointing to the elongated intertwined green structure with Tu in a circle on the top right bonding up and right to GTP Next to this is a smaller blue circle with AA2 inside. An elongated intertwined green structure with a blue circle representing AA2 joins this arrow. Below this image is a down arrow pointing to a replica of the first image described. This arrow is labeled as GTP hydrolysis and accommodation. This time, there is a second elongated intertwined green structure with AA2 in a blue circle on top. 
